  "agent": {
    "note": "candidate-002 feedback applied. (1) LEADERBOARD TOO DARK → the table panel now uses a distinct LIGHTER surface (#1c2433, like Beat 2's chart bg) so it reads as a panel; the row bands blend against it via a new table washColor prop (transparent surface kept, so panels still align). (2) KPI TEXT TOO SMALL → the stat-card sizes ALL its fonts off CARD HEIGHT, so wide-short cards = tiny text. Fixed by making the rail cards taller / more square: DESKTOP rail is now 2x2 (was 1x4 wide-short — this is the lever for bigger text you asked for; the 1x4 strip can't grow text without dropping cards); SQUARE 2x2 with the table trimmed so cards are taller; MOBILE is now a 4x1 row of TALL cards (was a 2x2 of wide-short tiles) — numbers 127/19/18.5K/9.7K are now prominent. Standalone table output unchanged (16 tests green). Renders: /tmp/b3d4.mp4, /tmp/b3s4.mp4, /tmp/b3m4.mp4.",
    "question": "Leaderboard panel lighter enough? KPI cards big enough now (desktop 2x2 vs the 1x4 you were comfortable with — the 2x2 is what makes the text bigger)? Mobile rail labels are still small relative to the numbers — want me to push those bigger too, or good to lock Beat 3?",
